ject." "Markkanen" Relocation 3s (3x10 shots): Shoot from one spot, then quickly relocate to another spot on the arc (e.g., wing to corner, top to wing) and catch-and-shoot. Progression: Perform with a time constraint (e.g., shoot 10 threes in 60 seconds from random spots). Coaching Cues: "Move with purpose, hands ready." "Be shot-ready on the catch." Cool-Down (10 minutes):  Static Stretches: Triceps stretch, chest opener, hamstring on wall, hip flexor stretch. Hold each for 20-30 seconds. Deep Breathing: 2 minutes of controlled diaphragmatic breathing. DAY 4: Game Flow, Court Mapping & Decision-Making Objective: Develop advanced court awareness, rapid decision-making under pressure, and the ability to dictate game tempo to enter flow states quickly.  Warm-Up (15 minutes):  Dynamic Stretching (5 min): Same as Day 1. Ball Handling - Eyes Up (5 min): Continuous dribbling (crossovers, between legs) while actively scanning and pointing to imaginary teammates or defensive positions on the walls of your space. Agility & Reaction (5 min): Mirror Drill: Simulate guarding an imaginary offensive player, reacting to their movements. (2x1 min) Cone React: Set up 2-3 cones. Dribble, then react to a visual cue (e.g., flash a number of fingers) by dribbling to a specific cone and executing a move. Main Block (75-90 minutes):  Court Mapping & Vision Drills (30 minutes):  "LeBron" Read & React Dribbling (3x2 min): Dribble continuously, calling out imaginary defensive positions (e.g., "help side," "on-ball," "backdoor cut") or offensive options ("kick out," "post entry," "floater"). Progression: Use colored cones as "defenders" and react based on their "position." Coaching Cues: "Head on a swivel. See the whole court, even if it's imaginary." "Process information and make decisions in real-time." Pass Out of Drive/Shot Simulation (3x10 reps): Drive hard towards the hoop, simulate a defender cutting off your path or rotating help, then simulate a pass to an imaginary open teammate (no actual pass, just the motion). Finish with a quick pivot or shot if no pass. Progression: Incorporate a shot fake before the simulated pass. Coaching Cues: "Drive with purpose, but read the defense as you go." "Eyes up before your gather for the shot." "Deliver a crisp, imaginary pass." Transition Reads (3x2 min): Simulate grabbing a rebound, then sprinting up the court while scanning for imaginary teammates and calling out potential options (e.g., "fast break left wing," "trailer," "early post"). Finish with a quick drive or pull-up. Progression: Alternate between being the primary ball-handler and a wing runner. Coaching Cues: "Push the pace, but keep your head up." "Make the easy read first." P&R Decision-Making (30 minutes):  Basic P&R Reads (3x8-10 reps each side): Dribble towards an imaginary screen, practice reads: "Go Over" (drive off screen, pull-up/floater) "Reject" (drive opposite of screen, attack rim) "Pocket Pass" (simulate pass to rolling big, then shoot if space) Progression: Add a "McCollum" re-screen or ghost screen simulation. Coaching Cues: "Be patient, let the screen develop." "Read the screener's defender's feet." "Make a decisive move, don't hesitate." P&R Counter Moves (3x8-10 reps): Drive off screen, defender recovers, hit a step-back midrange or 3-pointer. Progression: If the defender hedges high, practice a hard drive and finish. Coaching Cues: "Your counter is based on the defense's reaction." "Stay low and powerful through the counter." Game Flow Acceleration (15-30 minutes):  Continuous Offensive Moves (3x2-3 min): Continuous dribbling and stringing together offensive moves without stopping: e.g., crossover, then step-back, then drive, then floater, then retreat dribble, then jab-and-go. Keep moving, keep changing pace, keep reacting to imaginary defense. Progression: Add a condition: "If you hit the rim, you must do a push-up." Coaching Cues: "Flow like water. No wasted motion, no pauses." "Stay in attack mode, but control the tempo." "Anticipate your next move before you finish the current one." "LeBron" Multi-Option Finish (3x10 reps): Drive to the basket. Simulate passing, then shot-faking, then finishing with a tough layup or floater. Focus on keeping options alive. Progression: Perform with a timer to simulate game pressure. Coaching Cues: "Keep your head up through the entire drive." "Be a threat to pass, shoot, or drive simultaneously." Cool-Down (10 minutes):  Static Stretches: Piriformis stretch, figure-four stretch, hamstring stretch, glute stretch. Hold each for 20-30 seconds. Deep Breathing: 2 minutes of controlled diaphragmatic breathing. DAY 5: Post Play, Floaters & Advanced Finishing Objective: Develop a robust back-to-the-basket and face-up post-game, master the floater from various angles, and refine advanced finishing techniques for high-percentage scoring.  Warm-Up (15 minutes):  Dynamic Stretching (5 min): Same as Day 1. Mikan Drills (5 min): Classic Mikan drill (alternating hands on each side of the hoop) for 2 minutes. Focus on quick hands and soft touch on the tight rim. Footwork Prep (5 min): Drop Step Pivots: Practice drop steps with both feet, simulating sealing a defender. (5 reps each side) Face-Up Pivots: Practice facing up from the post, then pivoting to create space. (5 reps each side) Main Block (75-90 minutes):  "Brunson" Post Play & Footwork (30 minutes):  Basic Drop Step Finishes (3x10 each side): Start with back to the hoop, 5-8 feet out. Dribble once, drop step to the baseline, finish with a layup or short hook. Progression: Add a pump fake before the drop step. Coaching Cues: "Establish deep post position." "Powerful drop step, create space." "Use your body to protect the ball from imaginary defenders." Face-Up Series (3x10 each side): Start with back to the hoop. Pivot to face the hoop. Jab-and-Go: Fake one way, drive the other. Up-and-Under: Fake shot, then step through and finish. Rip-Through Drive: Catch, rip through low, drive hard. Progression: Combine two moves (e.g., jab-fake, then up-and-under). Coaching Cues: "Strong pivot to face up." "Sell the fake with your eyes." "Be explosive out of the face-up." Spin Move Finishes (3x8 each side): Dribble into the post, spin off an imaginary defender, finish at the rim. Progression: Add a counter if the spin is cut off (e.g., reverse pivot). Coaching Cues: "Low, quick spin." "Protect the ball, keep it tight." "Brunson" Floater Game Refinement (30 minutes):  Floater from Drive (3x10 each side): Dribble from 10-12 feet, drive towards the hoop, pull up for a floater from different angles (straight on, 45 degrees). Progression: Perform floaters off one foot vs. two feet. Coaching Cues: "High release, soft touch. Arc is key for the small rim." "Use your body to shield the ball." Floater with Contact (3x10 reps): Drive, simulate contact, and release the floater high and soft. Progression: Use a medicine ball or padded object for simulated contact. Coaching Cues: "Absorb the contact, stay strong, keep your eyes on the target." Floater off P&R (3x8 each side): Simulate P&R, drive into the lane, execute a floater over an imaginary big. Progression: Practice the floater after a sudden hesitation move. Coaching Cues: "Read the imaginary defender. High arc over the contest." Advanced Finishing Techniques (15-30 minutes):  Reverse Layups & Scoops (3x10 each side): Dribble drive, go under the hoop, and finish with a reverse layup or scoop shot. Focus on using the tight angles. Progression: Incorporate a spin move before the reverse. Coaching Cues: "Extend fully, use the glass for soft touch." "Protect the ball from imaginary shot blockers." Up & Under Finishes (3x10 each side): Drive, jump stop, pump fake high, then step through and finish low. Progression: Add a second pump fake if the first doesn't work. Coaching Cues: "Sell the shot fake." "Be quick and fluid with the step-through." "Markkanen" Versatile Finishes (3x10 reps): Work on various finishes that create space or get the 